  <section class="feat rev" id="torrents">
    <div class="wrap feat-in">
      <div class="feat-copy" data-reveal>
        <h2>Watch it while it is still downloading</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Pieces are prioritised around the playhead, and the seekbar shades what has already arrived, so you can see whether a jump will land or wait. A whole season is a queue you
          can start in seconds.
        </p>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
            <span><b>Nothing is downloaded until you ask for it</b>, and seeding is off by default, the one behaviour here with legal weight attached.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
            <span><b>Subtitles shipped inside the release are attached</b> by themselves, and the next episode is fetched ahead once the current one is complete.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
            <span><b>A stall says why.</b> Rate, peers and how much of this file is on disk, because "no peers" and "slow swarm" are different problems.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
